1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:02,270
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:02,340 --> 00:00:03,410
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,480 --> 00:00:05,180
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:07,980
(Episode 63)

5
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:22,890
This ends here.

6
00:00:47,190 --> 00:00:48,820
Did you really have to go this far?

7
00:00:51,560 --> 00:00:55,560
You think I stole
Kim Jung Sun's place, don't you?

8
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:57,060
Didn't you?

9
00:00:57,700 --> 00:00:59,560
How could you seduce my father?

10
00:00:59,560 --> 00:01:01,000
You didn't have to go this far.

11
00:01:01,470 --> 00:01:04,300
It was all mine to begin with.

12
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,200
What do you mean by that?

13
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:12,180
Director,

14
00:01:13,280 --> 00:01:14,610
I'm so sorry to ask,

15
00:01:15,550 --> 00:01:18,020
but could I adopt
that child instead?

16
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:21,150
But, ma'am...

17
00:01:21,550 --> 00:01:25,860
We already told Ae Sook
she was being adopted,

18
00:01:26,190 --> 00:01:28,060
and we even dressed her
in new clothes.

19
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:32,760
I feel like Ae Sook will get adopted
even if it isn't by me.

20
00:01:33,600 --> 00:01:34,900
I'm begging you.

21
00:01:35,670 --> 00:01:37,240
Please let me take
the other child instead.

22
00:01:37,740 --> 00:01:39,270
Kim Jung Sun and I...

23
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,710
grew up in the same orphanage.

24
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:45,740
I was supposed to be the one
adopted into Cheongma, not her.

25
00:01:46,710 --> 00:01:47,780
She stole...

26
00:01:48,410 --> 00:01:50,110
that chance from me.

27
00:01:51,150 --> 00:01:52,220
You're lying.

28
00:01:53,020 --> 00:01:55,690
That would mean Mom was an orphan
who got adopted.

29
00:01:58,420 --> 00:01:59,620
It's something...

30
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:01,830
you were bound to find out
sooner or later anyway.

31
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:08,400
So to take back that spot,

32
00:02:09,570 --> 00:02:11,170
you planted me at Cheongma?

33
00:02:12,640 --> 00:02:14,510
Just to satisfy your own greed?

34
00:02:15,270 --> 00:02:16,270
What?

35
00:02:16,710 --> 00:02:17,710
"Just?"

36
00:02:18,310 --> 00:02:19,910
Everything you have right now...

37
00:02:20,110 --> 00:02:22,550
was built with my blood,
sweat, and tears.

38
00:02:22,950 --> 00:02:25,320
Because I didn't want you
to suffer as an orphan...

39
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:28,050
or face the injustice
of having no education.

40
00:02:28,650 --> 00:02:30,690
I never wanted this from the start.

41
00:02:32,120 --> 00:02:33,120
I'm scared.

42
00:02:34,130 --> 00:02:35,660
I just want to walk away
from everything.

43
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:39,400
I'm so confused myself,
it's exhausting.

44
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:45,170
Kang Hae Ra, snap out of it.

45
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,070
Do you have any idea...

46
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:50,540
how many years I endured
just to put you in Cheongma?

47
00:02:51,940 --> 00:02:53,610
The finish line is
right before our eyes.

48
00:02:54,410 --> 00:02:55,680
Once we get past this hurdle,

49
00:02:56,150 --> 00:02:57,750
all of Cheongma will be yours.

50
00:03:01,920 --> 00:03:03,620
I'm just going
to tell Mom everything.

51
00:03:07,730 --> 00:03:10,230
I have dirt on Kang Young Hoon
that can destroy him...

52
00:03:10,230 --> 00:03:11,330
with a single blow.

53
00:03:11,660 --> 00:03:13,770
When the time is right,
I'll expose it all.

54
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:18,140
Only after Kim Jung Sun
and Kang Young Hoon fall...

55
00:03:18,370 --> 00:03:20,170
will Cheongma truly be yours.

56
00:03:22,240 --> 00:03:23,340
You decide.

57
00:03:24,440 --> 00:03:26,080
Will you rule Cheongma,

58
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:29,050
or be its abandoned daughter?

59
00:04:12,760 --> 00:04:17,500
(Mom)

60
00:04:37,620 --> 00:04:40,220
Meet Reporter Do Ji Hoon in person?

61
00:04:40,890 --> 00:04:41,890
Yes.

62
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:46,220
Will that reporter take our side?

63
00:04:47,290 --> 00:04:49,890
We'll get him on our side,
whatever it takes.

64
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:54,670
Since he only cares about money,
we definitely stand a good chance.

65
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:56,630
Still, Eun Seol,

66
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:02,310
could Director Joo
really have done it?

67
00:05:03,710 --> 00:05:05,640
No matter how much I think about it,

68
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:08,880
she'd never do
something like this to me.

69
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:13,720
I'm sure
it's hard to believe right now.

70
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:15,820
I understand.

71
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,920
Let's meet Reporter Do first...

72
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,860
and take our time
thinking it through.

73
00:05:35,470 --> 00:05:36,540
You decide.

74
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:39,340
Will you rule Cheongma,

75
00:05:40,550 --> 00:05:42,310
or be its abandoned daughter?

76
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:54,360
Hae Ra, don't worry too much.
I'm going to Eun Seol's place.

77
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:57,500
Reporters won't be able
to follow me there.

78
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,800
I'll be in touch.

79
00:06:23,490 --> 00:06:26,190
The sun feels nice today,
and so does the breeze.

80
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:28,730
- It's warm, isn't it?
- It really is.

81
00:06:31,030 --> 00:06:32,030
Isn't this too much trouble?

82
00:06:32,400 --> 00:06:34,300
Not at all. It's really no hassle.

83
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:36,000
You're the sweetest.

84
00:06:56,350 --> 00:06:57,720
I'll have it all.

85
00:06:58,590 --> 00:06:59,760
Mom, Dad,

86
00:07:00,420 --> 00:07:01,630
and even Cheongma.

87
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:11,300
Is Ko Eun Seol still not here?

88
00:07:11,570 --> 00:07:13,940
Eun Seol took the day off today.

89
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:15,270
Is she sick again?

90
00:07:15,710 --> 00:07:17,840
What happened to the main draft
that was supposed to be handed over?

91
00:07:19,510 --> 00:07:21,050
Wrap it up and submit it today.

92
00:07:22,280 --> 00:07:23,280
- Yes, ma'am.
- Yes, ma'am.

93
00:07:28,220 --> 00:07:29,520
Yes, this is Kang Hae Ra.

94
00:07:29,650 --> 00:07:31,120
The CEO would like to see you.

95
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:35,530
It feels so empty around here
without my wife.

96
00:07:37,260 --> 00:07:38,860
Yes, indeed.

97
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
By the way,

98
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,730
who was chosen as the acting head
of the scholarship foundation?

99
00:07:44,600 --> 00:07:47,640
Someone needs to step up
to fill in for the Chairman.

100
00:07:49,770 --> 00:07:53,040
How about having Ms. Kang
take that on?

101
00:07:53,610 --> 00:07:54,610
Hae Ra?

102
00:07:55,850 --> 00:07:58,980
But she just started working
at the foundation.

103
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:01,590
The employees might
push back strongly.

104
00:08:02,720 --> 00:08:04,420
Hae Ra needs
to learn the ropes, too.

105
00:08:05,190 --> 00:08:08,290
That way, she can step into
the Chairman's role down the road.

106
00:08:10,660 --> 00:08:12,200
Well, that's true.

107
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,500
This is a good chance for Hae Ra...

108
00:08:14,930 --> 00:08:18,700
to gain hands-on experience
at the foundation, right?

109
00:08:19,370 --> 00:08:21,840
Director Joo,
you're always so thoughtful.

110
00:08:26,340 --> 00:08:28,380
Hey, come on in.

111
00:08:33,020 --> 00:08:34,620
Hae Ra, from now on,

112
00:08:34,990 --> 00:08:37,050
I want you to run
the foundation's operations.

113
00:08:38,190 --> 00:08:39,560
- Me?
- Yes.

114
00:08:40,490 --> 00:08:41,490
You know how soft-hearted...

115
00:08:42,190 --> 00:08:44,060
your mom is.

116
00:08:44,660 --> 00:08:46,530
You need to be there for her.

117
00:08:47,160 --> 00:08:49,700
Director Joo and I
will help you out,

118
00:08:50,070 --> 00:08:51,400
so don't worry too much.

119
00:08:58,680 --> 00:09:00,440
What should I start on first?

120
00:09:04,380 --> 00:09:07,350
Why don't we start
by taking another look at...

121
00:09:07,350 --> 00:09:10,390
the current correctional
rehabilitation program?

122
00:09:10,450 --> 00:09:11,660
Yes, that sounds good.

123
00:09:11,660 --> 00:09:13,420
Let's use this chance to reassess...

124
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:16,190
the scholarship program's
feasibility.

125
00:09:27,570 --> 00:09:31,080
Director Joo, I'm taking
a few more days to clear my head.

126
00:09:31,480 --> 00:09:32,880
Don't worry too much.

127
00:09:35,710 --> 00:09:37,550
Worry? Oh, please.

128
00:09:38,120 --> 00:09:41,020
While you're at it,
why don't you stay gone for good?

129
00:09:44,690 --> 00:09:46,790
Ma'am, did you call for me?

130
00:09:48,190 --> 00:09:51,360
About the scholarship program
the Chairman is moving ahead with.

131
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,560
You've already screened
the candidates, right?

132
00:09:54,270 --> 00:09:56,870
Yes, I finished
evaluating them last week.

133
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,070
Is there any of them...

134
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:00,640
we could use as bait?

135
00:10:00,770 --> 00:10:02,240
Like someone in urgent need of cash.

136
00:10:03,570 --> 00:10:05,840
May I ask what this is regarding?

137
00:10:06,280 --> 00:10:08,110
You saw the news
about the Chairman, right?

138
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:10,280
We need to take this chance...

139
00:10:10,650 --> 00:10:13,150
to completely scrap
the scholarship program.

140
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,360
Jun Hwan.

141
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:24,360
The Chairman has to fall
if we're going to survive.

142
00:10:25,430 --> 00:10:26,660
And we have to survive...

143
00:10:27,430 --> 00:10:30,270
so what we did stays buried forever.

144
00:10:30,800 --> 00:10:31,800
Oh, right.

145
00:10:32,470 --> 00:10:33,470
Of course.

146
00:10:33,570 --> 00:10:36,640
This is no time to hesitate
and overthink things.

147
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:40,540
There's no other way for you and me.

148
00:10:41,250 --> 00:10:43,010
Do you understand what I'm saying?

149
00:10:44,520 --> 00:10:46,820
Yes, I understand.

150
00:10:49,250 --> 00:10:51,120
From the current
scholarship program,

151
00:10:51,190 --> 00:10:52,990
screen out candidates
who could be problematic.

152
00:10:53,790 --> 00:10:54,890
And among them,

153
00:10:54,990 --> 00:10:58,030
set up the most desperate one.

154
00:10:58,300 --> 00:11:00,060
Yes, I'll get right on it.

155
00:11:16,280 --> 00:11:18,620
Don't trust Director Joo too much.

156
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:21,990
You might end up regretting it.

157
00:11:28,590 --> 00:11:31,430
The Chairman has to fall
if we're going to survive.

158
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:33,960
And we have to survive...

159
00:11:34,370 --> 00:11:37,170
so what we did stays buried forever.

160
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:51,520
Hello?

161
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:53,220
Hello.

162
00:11:54,190 --> 00:11:56,220
Is this Mr. Park Ho Jun?

163
00:11:57,390 --> 00:11:58,590
Yes, speaking.

164
00:12:09,070 --> 00:12:11,070
This is the Cheongma
Scholarship Foundation.

165
00:12:12,840 --> 00:12:15,340
(Planning Director, Cha Seok Jin)

166
00:12:18,240 --> 00:12:19,480
Tae Seop...

167
00:12:20,280 --> 00:12:21,410
Oh Tae Seop.

168
00:12:22,850 --> 00:12:25,080
He is a bad man.

169
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:28,850
- A bad man?
- My darling...

170
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:33,820
He slammed into my darling
with a truck.

171
00:12:35,530 --> 00:12:36,590
Oh Tae Seop.

172
00:12:37,800 --> 00:12:39,560
I need to find out more.

173
00:12:42,430 --> 00:12:43,430
Come in.

174
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:48,410
- Chief Cha.
- Yes?

175
00:12:48,570 --> 00:12:50,010
The CEO is asking for you.

176
00:12:50,540 --> 00:12:51,540
Understood.

177
00:12:58,020 --> 00:13:01,050
I heard you went to see Director Oh.

178
00:13:03,050 --> 00:13:05,720
I wanted to ask for some help
before the gathering.

179
00:13:06,760 --> 00:13:09,960
Why Director Oh Tae Seop
of all people?

180
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:13,200
As far as I know,
you two aren't that close.

181
00:13:13,530 --> 00:13:15,270
Since he's close to you, sir,

182
00:13:15,330 --> 00:13:16,600
I wanted to ask for his advice.

183
00:13:17,270 --> 00:13:21,270
I wanted to take this chance
to get in your good graces.

184
00:13:23,740 --> 00:13:26,680
So there was no other reason?

185
00:13:28,350 --> 00:13:29,550
No, sir. None at all.

186
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:34,450
Brownie points? Please.

187
00:13:34,650 --> 00:13:36,350
Once you're part of Cheongma anyway,

188
00:13:36,420 --> 00:13:38,920
gatherings like this
will become routine.

189
00:13:40,560 --> 00:13:43,990
As one of your own,
I promise I won't let you down.

190
00:13:45,330 --> 00:13:46,330
Chief Cha,

191
00:13:47,130 --> 00:13:48,770
ease up a bit.

192
00:13:49,270 --> 00:13:50,430
Relax.

193
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:52,470
When you're that stiff,

194
00:13:52,540 --> 00:13:54,770
it's hard for people
to open up to you.

195
00:13:55,510 --> 00:13:57,980
We're going to be family soon,

196
00:13:58,740 --> 00:14:00,310
so it's time
we started getting closer.

197
00:14:01,910 --> 00:14:02,950
I'll try.

198
00:14:06,880 --> 00:14:07,890
By the way,

199
00:14:10,050 --> 00:14:11,720
about Director Oh Tae Seop...

200
00:14:15,430 --> 00:14:16,760
Never mind. It's nothing.

201
00:14:26,370 --> 00:14:28,940
(Chairman's Office)

202
00:14:42,850 --> 00:14:45,190
Have you thought about it,
Reporter Do?

203
00:14:48,060 --> 00:14:50,930
Director Joo Mi Ran is
a longtime client of mine.

204
00:14:51,700 --> 00:14:54,300
One of my VIPs, at that.

205
00:14:56,030 --> 00:14:57,200
So if Director Joo orders it,

206
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:59,940
you'll publish any article
without fact-checking?

207
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:05,410
Guess what gets tossed aside first
in this business.

208
00:15:06,510 --> 00:15:07,680
It's the facts.

209
00:15:09,410 --> 00:15:11,650
Because someone's
undeniable truth...

210
00:15:11,720 --> 00:15:14,750
can become an outright lie
from another angle.

211
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,720
You'd know,
since you've been through it.

212
00:15:24,660 --> 00:15:26,200
Reporter Do,

213
00:15:26,760 --> 00:15:28,530
now I finally see...

214
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:31,370
why you associate with Director Joo.

215
00:15:34,970 --> 00:15:35,970
So basically,

216
00:15:36,710 --> 00:15:38,980
you'll run any story
as long as the money's right.

217
00:15:39,810 --> 00:15:41,180
Is that what you're saying?

218
00:15:42,150 --> 00:15:43,210
As many as you like.

219
00:15:48,250 --> 00:15:49,390
When it comes to money,

220
00:15:54,060 --> 00:15:55,960
wouldn't I have more?

221
00:16:03,830 --> 00:16:06,400
Oh, right. Once we close up,
swing by my place.

222
00:16:06,840 --> 00:16:07,840
Sounds good.

223
00:16:07,910 --> 00:16:09,940
Let's finish up quickly
and grab a beer.

224
00:16:10,110 --> 00:16:11,110
That's not it.

225
00:16:11,180 --> 00:16:13,740
I made some side dishes,
so take them with you.

226
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:16,150
- Side dishes?
- Yes.

227
00:16:16,510 --> 00:16:18,250
Chairman Kim is still staying
with you.

228
00:16:18,520 --> 00:16:21,150
When you have a guest,
preparing meals is so stressful.

229
00:16:21,450 --> 00:16:23,890
I wanted to take that off your mind
tomorrow morning.

230
00:16:24,190 --> 00:16:26,360
I also made some soup,
so take that too.

231
00:16:27,930 --> 00:16:30,130
I really hit the jackpot with you.

232
00:16:31,160 --> 00:16:33,900
I mean, how did I find
such a perfect woman?

233
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:38,770
I really deserve some praise.

234
00:16:41,240 --> 00:16:42,270
What are you doing?

235
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:44,440
I'm just so proud of myself.

236
00:16:45,310 --> 00:16:48,250
Meeting you is the best thing
that's ever happened to me.

237
00:16:48,580 --> 00:16:49,980
Not so fast.

238
00:16:50,050 --> 00:16:52,020
You still have to get
your grandmother's approval.

239
00:16:52,220 --> 00:16:55,050
Who cares?
Let's just do what we want.

240
00:16:55,490 --> 00:16:58,360
What's with you? We can't do this.

241
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:00,760
Seriously, we can't.

242
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,160
Eun Seol,

243
00:17:02,790 --> 00:17:04,760
thank you
for all your hard work today.

244
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:07,060
Thanks to you,

245
00:17:07,430 --> 00:17:09,970
I was able to steady myself
when I was starting to waver.

246
00:17:11,440 --> 00:17:12,970
Honestly, lately,

247
00:17:13,240 --> 00:17:16,270
I've been thinking a lot
about Director Joo.

248
00:17:16,970 --> 00:17:18,010
Have you?

249
00:17:19,210 --> 00:17:21,810
Has Director Joo always been
this kind of person?

250
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:27,220
There were plenty of times
when I doubted her sincerity.

251
00:17:29,120 --> 00:17:30,190
Ma'am.

252
00:17:31,020 --> 00:17:32,020
Yes?

253
00:17:32,020 --> 00:17:33,590
This is only the beginning.

254
00:17:34,930 --> 00:17:38,230
Something even bigger could happen.

255
00:17:39,230 --> 00:17:41,170
So you must always...

256
00:17:42,030 --> 00:17:43,830
be on guard against Director Joo.

257
00:17:45,470 --> 00:17:46,470
I will.

258
00:17:49,240 --> 00:17:50,570
By the way, Eun Seol,

259
00:17:52,740 --> 00:17:54,180
why are you...

260
00:17:54,610 --> 00:17:56,880
going out of your way to help me?

261
00:18:02,190 --> 00:18:03,650
There's no other reason.

262
00:18:04,590 --> 00:18:06,820
I want to help,
simply because it's you.

263
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:09,790
And also,

264
00:18:10,160 --> 00:18:11,330
there's someone...

265
00:18:12,060 --> 00:18:13,630
I want to look into a bit more.

266
00:18:15,670 --> 00:18:16,930
Director Joo?

267
00:18:18,300 --> 00:18:20,070
To truly figure someone out,

268
00:18:20,270 --> 00:18:23,310
you have to look at them
from the opposite side.

269
00:18:23,870 --> 00:18:26,810
Why? Did something happen
with Director Joo?

270
00:18:28,610 --> 00:18:30,010
Once I'm more certain about it,

271
00:18:31,650 --> 00:18:33,080
I'll be sure to tell you.

272
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:38,260
All right. I'll wait until then.

273
00:18:42,630 --> 00:18:44,760
Thank you so much for everything.

274
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:47,830
Uncle, by any chance,

275
00:18:48,670 --> 00:18:50,370
do you remember
the name Oh Tae Seop?

276
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:51,840
Oh Tae Seop?

277
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:55,470
Right. He's the one
who caused your dad's accident.

278
00:18:55,770 --> 00:18:56,770
I remember.

279
00:18:57,510 --> 00:19:00,540
Do you remember anything else
about him?

280
00:19:01,210 --> 00:19:03,650
The vehicle
Oh Tae Seop was driving...

281
00:19:04,110 --> 00:19:07,150
belonged to a logistics center
run by a Cheongma subcontractor.

282
00:19:08,950 --> 00:19:11,260
A logistics center
for a Cheongma subcontractor?

283
00:19:11,320 --> 00:19:13,820
Yes. Your dad worked for Cheongma.

284
00:19:15,290 --> 00:19:17,960
Just his luck that he got hit
by a Cheongma vehicle.

285
00:19:19,860 --> 00:19:21,030
Then that means Oh Tae Seop...

286
00:19:21,370 --> 00:19:23,970
worked at a logistics center
run by a Cheongma subcontractor.

287
00:19:24,230 --> 00:19:25,970
Yes, most likely.

288
00:19:33,340 --> 00:19:35,310
For the time being, the Chairman...

289
00:19:35,380 --> 00:19:37,610
won't be able to handle
foundation affairs.

290
00:19:38,420 --> 00:19:41,020
In the meantime,
Ms. Kang will fill in for her.

291
00:19:44,220 --> 00:19:46,160
Who decided that?

292
00:19:46,460 --> 00:19:49,590
The Chairman left those instructions
before going on vacation.

293
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:52,800
Ko Eun Seol.

294
00:19:53,530 --> 00:19:54,730
Do you have a problem with that?

295
00:19:56,700 --> 00:19:57,730
No.

296
00:19:57,870 --> 00:19:59,870
As long as you can
take responsibility,

297
00:20:00,300 --> 00:20:02,240
as your subordinate,
I'll trust you and follow your lead.

298
00:20:04,580 --> 00:20:06,180
You'll trust me and follow my lead?

299
00:20:06,810 --> 00:20:08,210
Yes, of course.

300
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:12,580
If it came from the Chairman,
there must be a good reason for it.

301
00:20:14,020 --> 00:20:17,250
Then will Ms. Kang
be leading the meetings from now on?

302
00:20:18,020 --> 00:20:21,360
That's right. Though rather than
leaving it all to Ms. Kang,

303
00:20:21,660 --> 00:20:24,660
we should all work together
to get through this.

304
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:26,630
Right, Secretary Choi?

305
00:20:27,260 --> 00:20:30,170
Right, of course. I'll help as well.

306
00:20:30,730 --> 00:20:32,770
Please let me know
if you need anything.

307
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:35,370
I'll do my best to support you,
Ms. Kang.

308
00:20:44,950 --> 00:20:47,650
Then let's wrap up
today's meeting here.

309
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:49,120
Yes, ma'am.

310
00:20:59,500 --> 00:21:01,370
I noticed you took
the day off yesterday.

311
00:21:01,800 --> 00:21:03,130
Did something come up?

312
00:21:04,230 --> 00:21:08,370
No. Nothing special.
I just wanted to get some rest.

313
00:21:09,940 --> 00:21:12,040
I didn't know you had
this side to you, Eun Seol.

314
00:21:12,610 --> 00:21:14,480
You struck me as the type
to work even on weekends.

315
00:21:14,710 --> 00:21:16,380
I'm done living like that.

316
00:21:16,810 --> 00:21:19,080
I'll date and go shopping
like everyone else,

317
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,720
and do everything
I've never done before.

318
00:21:22,020 --> 00:21:23,620
I want to go on dates
with you often, too, Mom.

319
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:25,320
Well, yes,

320
00:21:25,320 --> 00:21:27,420
I suppose it's about time
you started enjoying life.

321
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:31,230
About the Chairman...

322
00:21:31,700 --> 00:21:33,500
What will happen once she returns?

323
00:21:34,330 --> 00:21:36,670
Considering what a big hit
she took from this incident,

324
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,300
it'll be hard for her
to run the foundation, right?

325
00:21:38,540 --> 00:21:39,770
I'd say so, wouldn't you?

326
00:21:40,270 --> 00:21:41,610
It's not just any position.

327
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:43,770
She's the Chairman
of the scholarship foundation.

328
00:21:44,470 --> 00:21:46,010
Someone like that abusing her power?

329
00:21:46,510 --> 00:21:48,450
For the foundation's
public image alone,

330
00:21:48,810 --> 00:21:50,550
she'll likely have to step back
from active leadership.

331
00:21:51,110 --> 00:21:53,320
Yes, I agree.

332
00:21:55,150 --> 00:21:56,390
Look at you,

333
00:21:57,020 --> 00:21:59,060
taking such an interest
in the company business.

334
00:21:59,890 --> 00:22:02,160
I should take an interest
in the company,

335
00:22:02,590 --> 00:22:04,160
if I want to follow
in your footsteps, Mom.

336
00:22:05,060 --> 00:22:06,060
In my footsteps?

337
00:22:06,630 --> 00:22:07,630
Yes.

338
00:22:07,900 --> 00:22:10,630
You're my role model, Mom.

339
00:22:22,480 --> 00:22:23,510
Ko Eun Seol.

340
00:22:24,180 --> 00:22:25,380
Do you have a problem with that?

341
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:27,850
No.

342
00:22:27,950 --> 00:22:30,050
As long as you can
take responsibility,

343
00:22:30,420 --> 00:22:32,290
as your subordinate,
I'll trust you and follow your lead.

344
00:22:41,360 --> 00:22:42,370
Ko Eun Seol.

345
00:22:48,210 --> 00:22:50,470
Here's the audit report
for the outsourced design services.

346
00:22:50,870 --> 00:22:52,680
Review it
and turn in your report today.

347
00:22:53,980 --> 00:22:56,010
Sure, I'll do that.

348
00:23:01,050 --> 00:23:02,050
Ko Eun Seol.

349
00:23:05,660 --> 00:23:08,330
Did my mom, I mean, the Chairman,

350
00:23:11,060 --> 00:23:12,460
reach out to you by any chance?

351
00:23:13,930 --> 00:23:16,170
No, she didn't.

352
00:23:31,450 --> 00:23:33,150
- Seok Jin.
- Yes?

353
00:23:33,650 --> 00:23:35,550
How high do you want to climb?

354
00:23:35,650 --> 00:23:36,720
What do you mean?

355
00:23:37,520 --> 00:23:39,460
I'm asking how high up
you want to go at Cheongma.

356
00:23:44,190 --> 00:23:45,730
I'm going to take it all.

357
00:23:47,230 --> 00:23:48,600
But it's tough to do alone.

358
00:23:49,270 --> 00:23:50,470
I need your help.

359
00:23:59,080 --> 00:24:00,080
Of course.

360
00:24:01,210 --> 00:24:03,210
We're going to spend
the rest of our lives together.

361
00:24:04,550 --> 00:24:06,080
No matter what happens,

362
00:24:07,180 --> 00:24:08,590
I'll defend my position.

363
00:24:13,020 --> 00:24:15,190
Like you, I want to be recognized
on my own merits.

364
00:24:16,590 --> 00:24:17,630
All right.

365
00:24:18,600 --> 00:24:19,730
I'll help you
with whatever you need,

366
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:21,160
so let me know
if anything gets tough.

367
00:24:22,270 --> 00:24:23,670
You have looked
a bit overwhelmed lately.

368
00:24:35,780 --> 00:24:37,850
My daughter is a bit slow
on the uptake, isn't she?

369
00:24:37,950 --> 00:24:39,620
I figured it out right away.

370
00:24:40,950 --> 00:24:42,190
Isn't it obvious?

371
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:43,890
She's that girl.

372
00:24:46,420 --> 00:24:47,560
The one you were swapped with.

373
00:24:48,230 --> 00:24:49,930
Ko Eun Seol.

374
00:24:51,030 --> 00:24:52,460
Cheongma's hidden daughter.

375
00:24:58,570 --> 00:25:00,170
She should've called by now.

376
00:25:01,100 --> 00:25:02,610
Why is it so quiet?

377
00:25:03,570 --> 00:25:06,140
I need to hit it big on this
and score a massive payday.

378
00:25:08,450 --> 00:25:10,950
Darn it, I'll just call first.

379
00:25:11,410 --> 00:25:15,250
If you want something done,
you have to do it yourself.

380
00:25:17,890 --> 00:25:20,560
(Head of Design Team, Kang Hae Ra)

381
00:25:25,800 --> 00:25:26,800
Hello?

382
00:25:27,630 --> 00:25:30,400
Sweetheart. Don't you miss your dad?

383
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:33,500
Shouldn't you be missing me by now?

384
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:35,610
I'm busy, so call me later.

385
00:25:36,140 --> 00:25:39,310
Goodness. My daughter must be busy.

386
00:25:39,580 --> 00:25:42,710
Why don't I drop by your work, then?

387
00:25:45,050 --> 00:25:46,350
Stay right where you are.

388
00:25:55,890 --> 00:25:58,860
Still, without the Chairman around,
doesn't it feel...

389
00:25:59,160 --> 00:26:00,200
a little empty around here?

390
00:26:02,270 --> 00:26:04,170
No, I actually feel more at ease.

391
00:26:04,900 --> 00:26:07,600
It feels as though things are
finally in their rightful place.

392
00:26:08,640 --> 00:26:09,810
How about you, Director Joo?

393
00:26:11,170 --> 00:26:13,440
Yes, I feel the exact same way.

394
00:26:14,780 --> 00:26:17,310
Once the scholarship scandal
we're working on blows up,

395
00:26:17,910 --> 00:26:19,980
she'll be sidelined even longer.

396
00:26:20,550 --> 00:26:21,650
Of course.

397
00:26:21,990 --> 00:26:25,220
I've already chosen the person
to use as bait.

398
00:26:25,590 --> 00:26:27,020
You never fail to impress.

399
00:26:30,230 --> 00:26:31,430
Come on, let's have a drink.

400
00:26:43,710 --> 00:26:46,180
Ramyeon really tastes best
right out of the pot.

401
00:26:48,480 --> 00:26:50,210
Did you call me here
just to watch you eat that?

402
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:55,490
Now that you know
who you were switched with,

403
00:26:56,390 --> 00:26:58,690
isn't it time for my princess
to make her move?

404
00:26:58,960 --> 00:27:00,660
What does that have to do with you?

405
00:27:01,190 --> 00:27:03,230
Why wouldn't it involve me, Hae Ra?

406
00:27:03,630 --> 00:27:05,460
I'm your father!

407
00:27:07,130 --> 00:27:09,370
I'll wire you some money,
so take it and get lost.

408
00:27:10,370 --> 00:27:13,070
Hae Ra, your dad
has plenty of money.

409
00:27:13,740 --> 00:27:15,370
Then what do you want?

410
00:27:16,940 --> 00:27:20,080
Forget the money.
Just upgrade my life a little.

411
00:27:21,180 --> 00:27:22,250
Hey, think carefully.

412
00:27:22,580 --> 00:27:24,810
Someone who'd do anything
for you and your mom?

413
00:27:25,350 --> 00:27:27,080
There's nobody else but me.

414
00:27:29,050 --> 00:27:31,150
Give me any task.
Your dad can do it all.

415
00:27:31,450 --> 00:27:32,660
I can do it!

416
00:27:37,460 --> 00:27:38,600
Sweetie, you're home.

417
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,200
Hey.

418
00:27:42,070 --> 00:27:43,430
Where's the Chairman?

419
00:27:43,970 --> 00:27:46,170
She stepped out for a bit
to take care of something.

420
00:27:46,400 --> 00:27:48,200
Did she mention where she was going?

421
00:27:48,270 --> 00:27:49,610
She didn't say anything like that.

422
00:27:50,070 --> 00:27:52,440
And it felt a bit awkward
to ask where she was going.

423
00:27:53,510 --> 00:27:55,380
- I see.
- Why worry about a grown woman?

424
00:27:55,380 --> 00:27:57,080
I'm sure she'll be back soon.

425
00:27:57,680 --> 00:27:59,350
But if you're worried,
give her a call.

426
00:28:07,390 --> 00:28:09,290
With that stuck-up freeloader here,

427
00:28:09,660 --> 00:28:12,930
this already cramped place
feels completely suffocating.

428
00:28:13,060 --> 00:28:16,500
Mom, can't you just
hold your tongue?

429
00:28:16,670 --> 00:28:19,740
We've got to stay
on Eun Seol's boss's good side.

430
00:28:19,800 --> 00:28:22,670
And what do we get out of it?
Any scraps for us?

431
00:28:22,910 --> 00:28:23,970
Who knows?

432
00:28:24,570 --> 00:28:26,210
Maybe she'll find Eun Guk...

433
00:28:26,910 --> 00:28:29,050
a desk in some corner
over at Cheongma.

434
00:28:29,250 --> 00:28:31,550
Wait. You have a point.

435
00:28:31,950 --> 00:28:36,350
You could ask her
to get you a job in security.

436
00:28:36,690 --> 00:28:37,850
Exactly.

437
00:28:37,920 --> 00:28:39,990
And maybe get you a spot
in the cafeteria, Mom.

438
00:28:40,060 --> 00:28:42,960
You brat, do you really have to
make me work there too?

439
00:28:45,130 --> 00:28:47,760
Ma'am, where are you right now?

440
00:28:48,730 --> 00:28:51,870
Eun Seol, I just stepped out
for a moment.

441
00:28:53,700 --> 00:28:56,040
Don't worry, I'll be back soon.

442
00:28:57,540 --> 00:28:59,940
All right. I'll call you later.

443
00:29:10,820 --> 00:29:11,920
Ma'am,

444
00:29:12,060 --> 00:29:15,590
would you like me to get you
the matching his-and-hers set?

445
00:29:16,830 --> 00:29:17,830
No.

446
00:29:18,660 --> 00:29:20,760
Just the women's, please.

447
00:29:21,260 --> 00:29:22,600
Yes, of course.

448
00:29:29,140 --> 00:29:32,840
Joo Mi Ran, I'm done
just sitting back and watching.

449
00:29:40,580 --> 00:29:42,650
Are you done packing, Mr. Seok Jin?

450
00:29:42,720 --> 00:29:43,720
Yes.

451
00:29:45,320 --> 00:29:48,290
This is your sportswear
for tomorrow.

452
00:29:48,360 --> 00:29:49,660
Right. Thanks.

453
00:29:51,360 --> 00:29:54,860
I think you're going to look
really handsome tomorrow.

454
00:29:56,070 --> 00:29:58,740
By the way, who are you
playing golf with?

455
00:29:59,200 --> 00:30:00,240
Are you going with Hae Ra?

456
00:30:01,470 --> 00:30:03,540
They're not really people
I'm comfortable around.

457
00:30:03,910 --> 00:30:07,380
If you're uncomfortable with them,
you don't have to go.

458
00:30:07,710 --> 00:30:08,810
There are people...

459
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:10,780
you have to put up with
even if it's uncomfortable.

460
00:30:12,550 --> 00:30:14,050
I also have some things
I really want to find out.

461
00:30:14,780 --> 00:30:17,050
Oh, I see.

462
00:30:17,520 --> 00:30:19,860
Then have a good time, Mr. Seok Jin.

463
00:30:24,030 --> 00:30:25,860
- Mom.
- Yes?

464
00:30:26,300 --> 00:30:28,230
If I can just make it through this,

465
00:30:29,170 --> 00:30:30,630
you might be able...

466
00:30:31,370 --> 00:30:32,570
to get your lost memories back.

467
00:30:34,800 --> 00:30:35,810
All right.

468
00:30:36,140 --> 00:30:38,610
Even if it's uncomfortable,
have fun.

469
00:30:39,140 --> 00:30:40,580
I'll be right here.

470
00:30:42,010 --> 00:30:44,050
Good luck, Mr. Seok Jin.

471
00:30:45,850 --> 00:30:46,880
Thanks, Mom.

472
00:30:49,590 --> 00:30:52,360
You were hitting it
really sharp today.

473
00:30:52,560 --> 00:30:54,320
Especially that birdie
on the last hole.

474
00:30:54,820 --> 00:30:57,630
That was truly spectacular. Right?

475
00:30:57,630 --> 00:30:59,830
Come on. I just got lucky.

476
00:31:00,960 --> 00:31:03,500
Anyway, thanks to Chief Cha,

477
00:31:03,700 --> 00:31:05,400
the energy was really great today.

478
00:31:07,440 --> 00:31:09,610
I mean,
it was Chief Cha's first round,

479
00:31:09,610 --> 00:31:11,770
- but his form looked great.
- Yes, exactly.

480
00:31:11,980 --> 00:31:14,380
- Did you take lessons?
- No, sir.

481
00:31:14,680 --> 00:31:16,710
It's all thanks
to the CEO's helpful pointers.

482
00:31:16,950 --> 00:31:18,380
Stop that.

483
00:31:18,820 --> 00:31:21,050
We should put a bet
on next month's round.

484
00:31:22,050 --> 00:31:23,190
A bet sounds good.

485
00:31:28,160 --> 00:31:29,160
Anyway,

486
00:31:29,330 --> 00:31:32,530
Oh Tae Seop is usually
glued to the CEO's side,

487
00:31:32,700 --> 00:31:33,860
so why didn't he show up today?

488
00:31:34,500 --> 00:31:35,500
Good point.

489
00:31:36,070 --> 00:31:38,570
Isn't this the first time
Oh Tae Seop sat one out?

490
00:31:40,500 --> 00:31:44,110
Could the CEO have left him out
on purpose?

491
00:31:44,740 --> 00:31:46,710
They were as thick as thieves.

492
00:31:46,840 --> 00:31:49,380
Do you think
Oh Tae Seop just got dropped?

493
00:31:51,350 --> 00:31:53,980
Did he leave out Oh Tae Seop
because of me?

494
00:31:55,790 --> 00:31:56,820
Chief Cha, hey.

495
00:31:57,450 --> 00:31:58,450
Over here.

496
00:31:58,790 --> 00:31:59,790
Oh, right.

497
00:32:01,020 --> 00:32:02,690
Where did my wife say she was?

498
00:32:03,760 --> 00:32:05,190
She said the villa felt stifling,

499
00:32:05,260 --> 00:32:07,060
so it seems she's resting
in Gangwon Province.

500
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:10,370
Right, Gangwon Province
has fresh air.

501
00:32:11,330 --> 00:32:13,070
She must be having
a good rest there.

502
00:32:15,200 --> 00:32:16,870
- Dad.
- Yes?

503
00:32:16,910 --> 00:32:18,240
I actually have something
to tell you.

504
00:32:19,580 --> 00:32:20,680
About Mom...

505
00:32:24,080 --> 00:32:25,110
What's going on?

506
00:32:28,790 --> 00:32:29,790
What...

507
00:32:32,060 --> 00:32:34,060
(Correction: Actress K's Ex-Manager
Denies Power Abuse)

508
00:32:45,500 --> 00:32:47,100
You all saw the news, right?

509
00:32:48,170 --> 00:32:49,270
Mom.

510
00:32:50,670 --> 00:32:53,840
Wait, how did you get here?

511
00:32:54,010 --> 00:32:56,710
I came with the person
who helped me.

512
00:32:57,180 --> 00:32:58,820
What do you mean,
the person who helped you?

513
00:32:59,780 --> 00:33:00,850
Come on in.

514
00:33:09,430 --> 00:33:10,430
Ko Eun Seol?

515
00:33:10,660 --> 00:33:13,560
Eun Seol helped me out
a lot this time.

516
00:33:45,930 --> 00:33:49,470
(A Trap Called Desire)

517
00:33:49,630 --> 00:33:52,870
Ko Eun Seol, how dare you
stab me in the back like this?

518
00:33:53,170 --> 00:33:55,640
You said to trust you.
You said you'd handle everything.

519
00:33:55,640 --> 00:33:57,210
You said you'd do anything
for me, right?

520
00:33:57,210 --> 00:33:58,980
Have you been meeting up
with An Guk Cheol?

521
00:33:58,980 --> 00:34:00,180
What's wrong? Shouldn't I?

522
00:34:00,240 --> 00:34:01,340
How dare she...

523
00:34:01,340 --> 00:34:03,250
Honey, how have you been?

524
00:34:03,250 --> 00:34:05,620
Was everything all right
while I was gone?

525
00:34:05,720 --> 00:34:09,050
Do you know anything about
my father's accident settlement?

526
00:34:09,050 --> 00:34:12,590
He thanked him
for killing my darling.

527
00:34:12,620 --> 00:34:14,790
Why are you working so hard
all of a sudden?

528
00:34:14,790 --> 00:34:16,360
I want to climb higher too.

529
00:34:16,360 --> 00:34:18,260
High up the ladder at Cheongma.

530
00:34:18,260 --> 00:34:20,230
I'm allowed to dream, aren't I?

531
00:34:20,360 --> 00:34:22,060
A dream of owning Cheongma.

532
00:34:22,970 --> 00:34:24,970
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
